-- TruthValues: The three truth values a membership question or condition can take: True, False, or NULL. Admitting NULL makes membership a partial, non-bivalent semantics rather than the classical two-valued one; bivalence is recovered wherever a definition is grounded.
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
